1. What belongs to the author. The source code, documents, data, models,
   images, sounds and other original materials in this repository and in the
   game published from it (together, "the Work") are authored by Matheus de
   Medeiros Pereira and are protected by Brazilian Law No. 9,610/1998
   (Copyright Law), Law No. 9,609/1998 (Software Law) and the applicable
   international treaties.

2. No license is granted. Viewing the code in a public repository or playing
   the published game grants no rights in the Work. Without the author's prior
   written permission, you may not:
   a) copy, reproduce or mirror the Work, in whole or in part;
   b) modify the Work or create derivative works from it;
   c) distribute, publish, sublicense, sell or make available the Work, or
      copies or derivatives of it, to third parties;
   d) use the Work for commercial purposes;
   e) use the Work, in whole or in part, to train, fine-tune, evaluate or feed
      artificial intelligence or machine learning models, including through
      automated collection (scraping) or text and data mining.

3. What does not belong to the author. The sprites, icons, backgrounds, sounds
   and names from Digimon UP and the Digimon franchise are NOT part of the
   project: they belong to their respective rights holders (Bandai Namco and
   licensors). They are not in this repository (they are kept out of git), they
   are used with the credit and provenance recorded in section 5.1 of
   docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md, and this license neither grants nor restricts any
   rights in them. The same applies to third-party libraries and assets, which
   remain under their own licenses.

4. No warranty. The Work is made available for reading "as is", without
   warranty of any kind.

5. Permission requests: through the author's GitHub profile (matheusmmmp).

In case of divergence between the two versions, the Portuguese version prevails.
Em caso de divergência entre as duas versões, prevalece a versão em português.
